Grotto Debian Packaging (Preview 0.1.0)
======================================

Build from a complete nostrc monorepo checkout with initialized submodules.
Use a clean source copy: the repository's root debian/ is a different,
headless package recipe. Replace it only in that disposable copy:

    cp -a apps/grotto/packaging/debian debian
    dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b

Install build dependencies from debian/control in the target distribution.
Supported floor is Ubuntu 24.04: GTK >=4.14, libadwaita >=1.5, GLib >=2.80.
Do not claim Ubuntu 22.04/Debian 12 support. Debian stable and Fedora target
acceptance is a separate owner decision. Build one deb per distro ABI; do not
assume a 24.04 binary installs on 26.04.

The single grotto_0.1.0-1_<arch>.deb includes GUI, daemon, both activation
services, Control1 XML, private JSON runtime library, icons,
schema, metainfo, opt-in autostart template, systemd user unit, network examples
and native-host assets. The Shell extension is an optional recommendation.
The old split grotto-daemon package is replaced, not newly emitted.

Build testing is OFF (a testing build must not be installed). Dedicated
Grotto CI runs the real private-bus signer/nip55l suites separately. Native
packaging uses CMake's apps/grotto component install. Do not substitute the
AppImage desktop file or legacy appdata XML. No login or network access is
automatically enabled; D-Bus activation starts the daemon on demand.
See ../README.md and ../../DAEMON_DEPLOYMENT.md for source/installed procedures.

Run lintian on the resulting package and follow docs/testing/grotto-manual-acceptance.md
before promotion. A successful package build is not installed-GNOME acceptance.
Flatpak/AppImage remain experimental with all five signer release gates open.
